#!/usr/bin/env python3
# =============================================================================
# ai-sandbox-web - loopback web dashboard for ai-sandbox --web sessions
#
# Lists, starts and stops sandboxes, and serves a browser terminal attached to
# the same zellij session a terminal client would attach to, so both are live
# read/write clients of one session.
#
# Deliberate constraints:
#   * Python standard library only. This project installs no runtime
#     dependencies, and adding a wheel supply chain to a tool whose purpose is
#     to reduce the trust surface would be self-defeating.
#   * No container port is ever published, and no host<->container network
#     plumbing is introduced. Containers are reached through `podman exec`,
#     exactly as a human at a terminal reaches them.
#   * Sessions are started by invoking `ai-sandbox`, never by building a
#     `podman run` command here, so container hardening stays single-sourced
#     and cannot be weakened from the web side.
#
# Usage: ai-sandbox-web [--addr ADDR] [--port PORT]
#        ai-sandbox web [...]        (same thing, via the wrapper)
# =============================================================================

